{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"771883f3c980c125","name":"card_unit_tupolev_sb_2","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_tupolev_sb_2","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"TUPOLEV SB-2","text":"Pincer: It costs the enemy +2 kredits to target or attack this unit.","flavorText":"The Tupolev SB-2 was a Soviet light bomber variant of the Tupolev ANT-40, used mainly by the Soviet Air Force during WWII. It played a significant role in the early stages of the war, particularly during the Soviet Union's defense against the German invasion. Developed in the late 1930s, the SB  was one of the most modern bombers of its time, featuring a streamlined design and advanced construction techniques. B It had a crew of three and was armed with machine guns for self-defense. By 1941, 94% of bombers in the Soviet Air Force were SB’s and it was employed in large numbers and proved to be effective against ground targets, enemy troop concentrations, and infrastructure. However, as the war progressed and German air superiority increased, the SB faced challenges. Its light armor and inadequate defensive armament made it vulnerable to enemy fire and the more advanced German fighters further reduced the bomber's effectiveness. Despite its limitations, the SB-2 remained in service throughout the war in various roles. It was used for reconnaissance, night bombing, and partisan support missions. Later in the war, as newer bombers became available, the Tupolev SB was gradually phased out of frontline service. A total of 6.656 SB’s were built, including quite a few variants.","faction":"Soviet","type":"bomber","rarity":"Rare","cost":6,"operationCost":2,"attack":5,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_tupolev_sb_2","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_tupolev_sb_2_title","SourceString":"TUPOLEV SB-2","LocalizedString":"TUPOLEV SB-2"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::bomber","attack":5,"defense":5,"range":2,"fac