f the most modern bombers of its time, featuring a streamlined design and advanced construction techniques. B It had a crew of three and was armed with machine guns for self-defense. By 1941, 94% of bombers in the Soviet Air Force were SB’s and it was employed in large numbers and proved to be effective against ground targets, enemy troop concentrations, and infrastructure. However, as the war progressed and German air superiority increased, the SB faced challenges. Its light armor and inadequate defensive armament made it vulnerable to enemy fire and the more advanced German fighters further reduced the bomber's effectiveness. Despite its limitations, the SB-2 remained in service throughout the war in various roles. It was used for reconnaissance, night bombing, and partisan support missions. Later in the war, as newer bombers became available, the Tupolev SB was gradually phased out of frontline service. A total of 6.656 SB’s were built, including quite a few variants."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"hasPincer":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion_Medium'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Explosion_Medium.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Soviet/Spring2023Candidates/t_tupolev_sb_2.t_tupolev_sb_2","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Jaroslaw Wróbel","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/TUPOLEV_SB-2.TUPOLEV_SB-2","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":256.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_tupolev_sb_2_photo","SourceString":"A Tupolev SB-2 of the Soviet Air Force. Date unknown. ","LocalizedString":"A Tupolev SB-2 of the Soviet Air Force. Date unknown. "},"blowUpExplosion":{"ObjectName":"ParticleSystem'P_ExplosionAircraftM'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Explosions/Medium/Aircraft/P_ExplosionAircraftM.193"},"blowUpC